# WPF Styling Standards

## Core Principle

**Readability always wins over branding.** If a brand/accent color reduces legibility, adjust its shade or switch to a neutral foreground.

## MahApps.Metro Integration

- Use `MetroWindow` as base window class (not `Window`)
- Reference MahApps resource dictionaries in `App.xaml`
- Use centralized `Resources/AppColors.xaml` for all brushes

## Contrast Rules

- Dark background (luminance < 0.4) → use near-white foreground (`#FFFFFF` or `#F5F5F5`)
- Light background (luminance >= 0.4) → use near-black foreground (`#1A1A2E` or `#212121`)
- NEVER: red text on blue/dark background, blue text on blue background
- Minimum contrast ratio: 4.5:1 (WCAG AA)
- Accent color for borders/icons/badges only — never body text unless contrast ≥ 4.5:1

## Centralized Color Resources

Never inline hex colors. Define in `Resources/AppColors.xaml`:

```xml
<!-- Backgrounds -->
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="AppBackgroundBrush" Color="#FAFBFC"/>
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="PanelBackgroundBrush" Color="#F5F7FA"/>
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="CardBackgroundBrush" Color="#FFFFFF"/>

<!-- Foregrounds -->
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="PrimaryTextBrush" Color="#1A1A2E"/>
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="SecondaryTextBrush" Color="#5A6270"/>

<!-- Selection: foreground MUST contrast with background -->
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="SelectedRowBackgroundBrush" Color="#1565C0"/>
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="SelectedRowForegroundBrush" Color="#FFFFFF"/>
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="HoverRowBackgroundBrush" Color="#E8EAF6"/>
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="HoverRowForegroundBrush" Color="#1A1A2E"/>
```

## DataGrid Selected/Focused States

Always override these triggers — default system colors clash:

```xml
<Style TargetType="DataGridCell">
  <Style.Triggers>
    <Trigger Property="IsSelected" Value="True">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource SelectedRowForegroundBrush}"/>
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource SelectedRowBackgroundBrush}"/>
    </Trigger>
  </Style.Triggers>
</Style>

<Style TargetType="DataGridRow">
  <Style.Triggers>
    <Trigger Property="IsSelected" Value="True">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource SelectedRowForegroundBrush}"/>
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource SelectedRowBackgroundBrush}"/>
    </Trigger>
    <Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource HoverRowBackgroundBrush}"/>
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource HoverRowForegroundBrush}"/>
    </Trigger>
  </Style.Triggers>
</Style>
```

## Rules

- Reference brushes via `{StaticResource BrushKey}`, never hardcode `#hex`
- Every `Background` setter must have paired `Foreground` with adequate contrast
- When overriding styles, always handle `IsSelected`, `IsMouseOver`, `IsFocused` with explicit foreground

## Checklist After Editing XAML

- [ ] No inline `#hex` colors — use `{StaticResource}`
- [ ] Every `IsSelected` trigger sets both Background AND Foreground
- [ ] Every `IsMouseOver` trigger sets both Background AND Foreground
- [ ] DataGrid cell text readable in all states: normal, hover, selected, editing
- [ ] Buttons with colored backgrounds have white or near-white foreground
